Summary: WINEDLLPATH_<renderer>: per-renderer DLL search paths set by the launcher
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: reconstructed
  Version: Sikarugir 10.0_8
  Binary: WS12WineSikarugir10.0_8 ntdll.so
  Functions: set_dll_path (inlined into init_paths, 0x1e312-0x1e835), the
    launcher check at 0x21900
  Changes: argv from ntdll's main_argc/main_argv instead of
    _NSGetArgc/_NSGetArgv (the same array on macOS: the preloader shifts argv
    in place); the launcher check runs once per variable that has an entry
    instead of once per entry (same result)
  Note: Sikarugir-only: no CrossOver 26, wine-staging or WineHQ equivalent
Upstream: no
Why: Lets the launcher script put each renderer's DLLs on Wine's DLL search
 path through its own variable (WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL, _CNCD, _D9VK, _DXVK,
 _DXMT, in that order), each a ':'-separated list of folders laid out like
 Wine's lib/wine (x86_64-windows, i386-windows, x86_64-unix). They're
 searched before Wine's own builtin directory and before WINEDLLPATH, so a
 renderer's d3d11.dll or dxgi.dll replaces Wine's. The D3DMetal, D9VK and
 DXVK lists are left out for launcher and overlay processes, matched by
 case-sensitive substring on argv[1], so their Chromium UIs keep using
 wined3d; the games they start still get them (shown on 10.0 build0: a
 Battle.net.exe got Wine's dxgi, its child D3DMetal's). With none of the
 variables set, the search path is unchanged.
Programs: Battle.net, EA app, Epic, EOS overlay, GOG Galaxy, Rockstar
 launcher/Social Club, Steam web helper and overlay, Ubisoft Connect: their
 Chromium UIs would get the D3DMetal, D9VK or DXVK DLLs instead of wined3d
Matches: exe Battle.net.exe, battlenet.overlay.runtime.exe,
 BlizzardBrowser.exe, BlizzardError.exe, EACefSubProcess.exe,
 EADesktop.exe, Link2EA.exe, EpicGamesLauncher.exe, EpicWebHelper.exe,
 EOSOverlayRenderer-Win32-Shipping.exe,
 EOSOverlayRenderer-Win64-Shipping.exe, GalaxyClient.exe, GalaxyClient
 Helper.exe, GOG Galaxy Notifications Renderer.exe, steamwebhelper.exe,
 gameoverlayui.exe, gameoverlayui64.exe, UbisoftConnect.exe,
 UplayWebCore.exe, UpcElevationService.exe; path Rockstar
 Games\Launcher\Launcher.exe, Rockstar Games\Social
 Club\SocialClubHelper.exe
Enable: env WINEDLLPATH_D3DMETAL=<d3dmetal>/wine (each process that has it)
 env WINEDLLPATH_CNCD=<folders> (each process that has it)
 env WINEDLLPATH_D9VK=<folders> (each process that has it; not launchers)
 env WINEDLLPATH_DXVK=<folders> (each process that has it; not launchers)
 env WINEDLLPATH_DXMT=<folders> (each process that has it)
Risk: loads DLLs from the folders the variables name, ahead of Wine's own;
 whoever sets the environment chooses them
Related: wine-inf-d3dmetal-placeholder-dlls, winemetal-stub; files in the
 prefix that let DLLs of those names on these paths load
Status: 10.0: 2026-11-26: header only. In build0

